  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Based on the post of Norbert Sándor to the user list:<br/>
<br/>
When printing a 198.425 x 1700.787 sized page (70 x 600 mm) using new PDFPrinter(pdfDocument, printJob).silentPrint() to a virtual printer (e.g. PDFCreator or CIB), then the resulting PDF has a page size of 8,26x11,69 and the content is horizontally centered on the page. I was able to reproduce the problem, and also to print on a virtual printer that creates new PDFs of that size, by using the longest constructor of PDFPrinter(), but then the output is blank.<br/>
<br/>
While it doesn&#39;t seem useful to print a PDF to a PDF, the problem might make sense when printing to a cash register receipt printer.
