                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-2310,                                                PDFBOX-2313,                                                PDFBOX-2323,                                                PDFBOX-1462,                                                PDFBOX-626,                                                TIKA-1375,                                                TIKA-1294                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 7<br/>
java version &quot;1.7.0_55&quot;<br/>
Java(TM) SE Runtime Environment (build 1.7.0_55-b13)<br/>
Java HotSpot(TM) 64-Bit Server VM (build 24.55-b03, mixed mode)<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      ExtractImages seems to fail to release memory resources on some files in both PDFBox 1.8.5 and trunk.  <br/>
<br/>
On this file 4MB file [http://digitalcorpora.org/corp/nps/files/govdocs1/239/239665.pdf], if extracting every image on every page (and there are many, many duplicate images), there is an OOM with -Xmx1g.  If there is no Xmx and there is &gt; 2.5g available, ExtractImages will work.<br/>
<br/>
With some experimentation, the triggers seem to be JPEG images that have masks.  I&#39;m not sure, though, whether the issue is with PDFBox or Java.<br/>
<br/>
Commandlines:<br/>
1.8.5:<br/>
java -Xmx1g -cp pdfbox-app-1.8.5.jar org.apache.pdfbox.ExtractImages 239665.pdf<br/>
<br/>
2.0_SNAPSHOT:<br/>
java -Xmx1g -cp pdfbox-app-2.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar org.apache.pdfbox.tools.ExtractImages -addkey 239665.pdf<br/>
<br/>
