                <tr id="issuerow12722715" rel="12722715" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-2153" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-2153" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-2153">PDFBOX-2153</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Setting the correct clipping path for shading
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 20/Jun/14 07:01 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Sep/14 14:40 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 22/Jun/14 16:29 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.5,                     1.8.6,                     1.8.7,                     2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.8.7,                     2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Rendering            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        PDFBOX-1451,                                                PDFBOX-1947                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      While doing tests with the file eci_altona-test-suite-v2_technical_H.pdf (uncompressed) of PDFBOX-1915 I noticed that by removing a &quot;W&quot; (modifies the clipping region) operator of a type 7 shading I got a lot more correct shadings (type 6 and lower). It looked like PDFBox had been using the clipping of the type 7 when drawing the type 6, which is just a rectangle above in that rendering. This resulted in a blank.<br/>
<br/>
By adding <br/>
{code}<br/>
graphics.setClip(getGraphicsState().getCurrentClippingPath());<br/>
{code}<br/>
in PageDrawer.shfill() just before the graphics.fill() I get several files to render correctly that I hadn&#39;t before.<br/>
<br/>
(Setting null will probably do the same, didn&#39;t test that yet).<br/>
<br/>
The following PDFs are rendered correctly with the change:<br/>
McAfee-ShadingType7.pdf<br/>
eci_altona-test-suite-v2_technical_H.pdf<br/>
crestron-p9.pdf  (these three found in PDFBOX-1915)<br/>
PDFBOX-1451.pdf (&quot;alfresco&quot;)<br/>
PDFBOX-1940.pdf (&quot;chart&quot;)<br/>
PDFBOX-1861-tracemonkey.pdf p.11<br/>
<br/>
Not solved by the change:<br/>
PDFBOX-2098-asyTUG.pdf p.6  (this one doesn&#39;t use shfill)<br/>
PDFBOX-1861-tracemonkey.pdf p.6 (not shading)<br/>
PDFBOX-1416.pdf (not shading)<br/>
texample-rgb-triangle.pdf (John has an explanation about that one)<br/>
<br/>
WDYT? Is there any reason NOT to set the clipping path in PageDrawer.shFill() ?
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    shading, shadingpattern</td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310220">            <span title="20/Jun/14 08:55"><time class="livestamp allow-future" datetime="2014-06-20T08:55:01+0000">20/Jun/14 8:55 AM</time></span>
    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312322"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312520"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312323"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312521">    3 years, 2 days ago

                        </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312320"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310420">      400906
  </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312321"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312120">
</td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312121"><span class="sla-agent-restricted">Restricted to agents</span>
</td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312328"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312329"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312326"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312327"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312720"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312324"></td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12312325"></td>
