</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In some right-to-left languages, compound words are separated using &quot;semi-space&quot; (please take a look at Unicode spaces: https://www.cs.tut.fi/~jkorpela/chars/spaces.html). When the input document contains these words, PDFTextStripper neglects semi-space character and concatenates words together. 
  </td>
