</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The BufferedImages for flate encoded images seem to be defective. The following code results in a ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException when writing the image:<br/>
{code}<br/>
PDDocument doc = PDDocument.load(&quot;test.pdf&quot;);<br/>
Iterator&lt;PDXObject&gt; it = doc.getPage(0).getResources().getXObjects().values().iterator();<br/>
PDImageXObject image = (PDImageXObject) it.next();<br/>
BufferedImage bi = image.getImage();<br/>
try (FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(&quot;test.bmp&quot;)) {<br/>
    ImageIO.write(bi, &quot;bmp&quot;, fos);<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
The problem did not exist in 1.8. The attached PDF just contains one flate encoded image.
  </td>
