                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Marc Davis fronm the user mailing list has provided a file (michael levine.pdf) that, when merged with another file, has a black image on page 17 (&quot;TL-9&quot;). I tried to investigate / narrow this somewhat:<br/>
- it happens with any other file, or just use the michael levine file twice<br/>
- extracting p17 with PDFSplit and then merging the result doesn&#39;t do it<br/>
- extracting p1-17 with PDFSplit  and then merging the result does do it<br/>
- extracting p13-17 with PDFSplit  and then merging the result does do it, altthough the black is now at the first page<br/>
<br/>
The page is not really &quot;black&quot;, the colors are incorrect.<br/>
<br/>
That&#39;s all I found out until now. I compared the two files with PDFDebugger and can&#39;t see any obvious differences. I looked into the files with NOTEPAD++, there are some differences like that the colorspace is now indirect.
