                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 8, Java 7
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      In v 1.8, if you set a PDPageable to a PrinterJob and told it to print(), it would print AcroForm fields if they existed.<br/>
Now, with PDFPrinter (a great improvement in many respects!) the AcroForm fields don&#39;t print anymore.<br/>
I have tried pinpointing the problem in PDFPrinter, PDFRenderer, and PageDrawer, but unsuccessfully.<br/>
Perhaps I am doing it wrong.  Here is some code:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
PDAcroForm form = document.getDocumentCatalog().getAcroForm();<br/>
PDFieldTreeNode f = form.getField(&quot;referral&quot;);<br/>
f.setValue(&quot;test&quot;);<br/>
PDFPrinter pdfPrinter = new PDFPrinter(document);<br/>
pdfPrinter.silentPrint();<br/>
{code}
