</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      While working on PDFBOX-2660 I discovered that PDGraphicsState#intersectClippingPath performs a shallow copy of the Area, which means that it will retain any mutation which occurs in following states.<br/>
<br/>
I don&#39;t have a PDF file which is known to trigger this problem, but I&#39;ve confirmed that it exists with a debugger.
  </td>
