</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      For navigating first page and last pages of a pdf file, there is no keyboard shortcut like other PDF readers. It&#39;s a simple yet intuitive functionality for any PDF reader. <br/>
Generally ctrl+End, End are used to jump to the last page while ctrl+Home, Home are used to jump to the first page. <br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve written a patch for this.<br/>
In View menu, two new entry is added i.e &quot;First page&quot;, &quot;Last Page&quot; along with keyboard shortcuts. And view menu items are made responsive e.g.  when I&#39;m in the first page &quot;previous page&quot; and &quot;first page&quot; menu entries are disabled. 
  </td>
