                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;ve found an issue with RandomAccessBuffer which is triggered in a very specific corner case only:<br/>
- the buffer has more than 1 chunk<br/>
- read(byte[] b, int offset, int length) is used to read the data<br/>
- the data is read in portions<br/>
- one of the portions to be read is identical with the last remaining bytes of the current chunk<br/>
The current implementation won&#39;t advance to the next buffer, but reads the last bytes again and again.<br/>

  </td>
