                <tr id="issuerow12839325" rel="12839325" data-issuekey="PDFBOX-2837" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    PDFBox
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="PDFBOX-2837" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-2837">PDFBOX-2837</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                PDFBox creates files with EBCDIC code on z/OS
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Tilman Hausherr
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 20/Jun/15 10:30 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Jul/15 06:35 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 22/Jun/15 06:36 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.8.9,                     1.8.10,                     2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.8.10,                     2.0.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Writing            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      OS: Unix Service running on Z/OS.<br/>
JRE: JRE 1.6.0 IBM J9 2.4 z/OS s390-31 
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      A PDF file created on z/OS (an IBM mainframe os) has this<br/>
{code}<br/>
xref<br/>
ð ù<br/>
0000000000 65535 f<br/>
{code}<br/>
the two chars are EBCDIC code for 0 9. The cause is this code that outputs in the system default encoding:<br/>
{code}<br/>
    private void writeXrefRange(long x, long y) throws IOException<br/>
    {<br/>
        getStandardOutput().write(String.valueOf(x).getBytes());<br/>
        getStandardOutput().write(SPACE);<br/>
        getStandardOutput().write(String.valueOf(y).getBytes());<br/>
        getStandardOutput().writeEOL();<br/>
    } <br/>
{code}<br/>
getBytes should use the specific charset, e.g. getBytes(Charsets.ISO_8859_1).
  </td>
