                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        TIKA-1285                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m about a quarter of the way through the run against govdocs1 with 2.0.0 trunk.  The log file (threshold=error) for pdfbox alone weighs in at 2 GB.  It looks like there is quite a bit of logging along the lines of:<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
1488429 2015-07-08 19:44:49,460 [pool-2-thread-14] ERROR org.apache.pdfbox.pdmodel.font.FontMapper  - Using last-resort fallback for TTF font &#39;Times-Roman&#39;<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
Are these truly &quot;error&quot; level events?  If so, should they be happening this often?  I realize govdocs1 is an aging corpus...<br/>
<br/>
On a recent run with 1.8.9, the pdfbox&#39;s error log file was 6.5MB.
  </td>
