</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows 8<br/>
$ java -version<br/>
java version &quot;1.8.0_40&quot;<br/>
Java(TM) SE Runtime Environment (build 1.8.0_40-b26)<br/>
Java HotSpot(TM) 64-Bit Server VM (build 25.40-b25, mixed mode)
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I use the PDFRender in my application and noticed that the renderImageWithDPI method throws an exception with certain pdf files. The bug can be reproduced with the pdfbox-app  command below. The medibank.pdf file is available via my Google Drive account:<br/>
https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B7b7_UXpgIdGb2djYTNDNmVtVTA/view?usp=sharing<br/>
<br/>
$ java -jar pdfbox-app-2.0.0-20150819.113526-1604.jar PDFToImage medibank.pdf<br/>
Aug 20, 2015 3:53:43 PM org.apache.pdfbox.rendering.TTFGlyph2D getPathForGID<br/>
