                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the method printWithPaper of  Printing.java example,<br/>
if I use java.awt.print.Book as in the example:<br/>
Book book = new Book();<br/>
book.append(new PDFPrintable(document), pageFormat);<br/>
job.setPageable(book);<br/>
<br/>
when I execute job.print(); it print only the first page of the document.<br/>
<br/>
I solved this issue by replacing the three rows mentioned above with:<br/>
job.setPrintable(new PDFPrintable(document), pageFormat);<br/>
<br/>
by that all pages are printed.<br/>
<br/>
I hope this is useful for someone.<br/>
<br/>
Matteo<br/>

  </td>
